.TH XYMON-PLUGIN 8 "November 23, 2026" "xymon-plugins"
.SH NAME
xymon-plugin \- install, update and check the Xymon plugins, itself among them
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "xymon-plugin install|update|enable|disable|remove|status|verify|outdated|clean [--server|--client|--tools] [--all] [PLUGIN...] [NAME=value...]"
.br
.B "xymon-plugin --version"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xymon-plugin
installs each plugin of the xymon-plugins repository from its
.I PLUGIN
file: on a Xymon server under
.IR $XYMONHOME/ext/NAME/ ,
elsewhere under
.IR $PREFIX/libexec/xymon-plugins/NAME/ .
It is run from a checkout or a release's archive as
.BR ./xymon-plugin ,
a link to
.IR plugins/xymon-plugin/xymon-plugin .
.PP
It is a plugin itself:
.B "./xymon-plugin install --server xymon-plugin"
installs it into
.I $XYMONHOME/ext/xymon-plugin/
with its
.IR PLUGIN ,
.I VERSION
and
.I MANIFEST
files, so that
.B status
and
.B outdated
report its own version beside the others'. On a monitored host,
.B "./xymon-plugin install --client xymon-plugin"
installs it the same way into a standalone Xymon client's
.IR ext/xymon-plugin/ ,
with the client's plugins column (below). The copy installed gives its
version, and runs
.BR status ,
.B verify
and
.B outdated
on what is installed; it holds no plugin, so
.B status
says of each that it is not in this copy. To install or update plugins,
run the checkout's or the archive's.
.PP
Every verb and setting is described in
.IR plugins/xymon-plugin/README.md ,
the short version in
.IR plugins/README.md .
.SH THE PLUGINS COLUMN
Installed on a server, it brings a task, off until
.B "./xymon-plugin enable --server xymon-plugin"
turns it on. Once a day, after a wait drawn at random up to 6 hours, its
reporter,
.IR xymon-plugin-report.sh ,
runs again from its file when it waited, so that an update during the wait has its code
send, then runs the installer installed beside it,
.BR "outdated --server" ,
and sends the server's status
.BR plugins ,
valid 31 hours, with
.BR outdated 's
lines, each plugin's with the icon of its colour, under a first line that
counts the plugins and names those behind: green when no newer release of a plugin installed is published;
yellow when one is, a plugin's
.I VERSION
cannot be compared, or
.B outdated
ends otherwise; nothing when GitHub is not reached, so that the status goes
purple once 31 hours have passed since the last one, as when a restart of
xymond stops the task while it waits. It reads GitHub with
.BR curl ,
bounded in time, not
.BR gh .
The status is for
.BR MACHINEDOTS ,
the server's name in
.IR xymonserver.cfg ,
which
.I hosts.cfg
must name; read back, one that xymond did not keep is said, and the
reporter ends with 1. Its log is
.IR xymon-plugin.log ,
in Xymon's log directory. Yellow and purple alert as any column:
.B EXSERVICE=plugins
in
.I alerts.cfg
keeps it out of a rule.
.PP
With the task on, an
.BR install ,
.B update
or
.B remove
of the server part that changed a plugin, and the
.B enable
of this plugin, its task on already or not, send the column at once, by the
reporter with no
wait, under
.BR xymoncmd ,
and say what was sent, or why nothing was; the command's own exit does not
depend on it. Under
.B DESTDIR
nothing is sent. So
.B enable --server xymon-plugin
is the way to have the column sent now, a release published since its last
run among what it says.
.PP
On a standalone client, its task, off until
.BR "./xymon-plugin enable --client xymon-plugin" ,
runs the same reporter with
.BR --client ,
under
.IR xymonclient.cfg :
.B "outdated --client"
asks GitHub from the client itself, and the client's status
.B plugins
goes to its server. The status is for
.B MACHINEDOTS
as
.I runclient.sh
gives it, its
.B --hostname
or the system's name, written by the task each run in
.IR $XYMONTMP/xymon-plugin.host ;
the log is
.I xymon-plugin.log
in
.BR XYMONCLIENTLOGS .
The column is sent at once as on the server, under the name that file
holds or, before any run, the one in
.IR logs/clientlaunch.NAME.pid ;
with neither, nothing is sent, and the command says so. GitHub allows 60
anonymous requests an hour from one address, which bounds how many clients
behind one address can ask it each day.
.PP
On a server as on a client, where
.B XYMSRV
is 0.0.0.0 the status goes to each server
.B XYMSERVERS
names, each read back for that host and that column alone: one that did
not keep it is said and ends the run with 1; kept blue, the column
disabled, it is said, and does not; one that refuses to show its board to
this host (xymond's
.BR --www-senders )
is said, and does not \(em whether it kept the status is then not known,
nor, on a xymond that knows no host at all, told apart from a refusal.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --version
The installer's version: its
.I PLUGIN
file's, beside it when installed, under
.I plugins/xymon-plugin/
in a checkout or an archive.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B https_proxy, GH_TOKEN
Read by the task where a file under
.I xymonserver.d/
sets them: the proxy to reach GitHub, and a token, which
.B curl
is given on its standard input.
.TP
.B XYMON_PLUGINS_WAIT, XYMON_PLUGINS_TIMEOUT
The reporter's longest wait, and the bound of each request
.B curl
or GNU
.B wget
makes, in seconds: for the tests.
.B gh
has none; the task leaves it out
.RB ( XYMON_PLUGINS_NO_GH ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on an error, 2 for a usage error;
.B verify
ends with 3 when something is broken and 4 when it is only untidy,
.B outdated
with 7 when a plugin's
.I VERSION
cannot be compared, else 6 when a newer release exists, as
.I plugins/xymon-plugin/README.md
says.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XYMONHOME/ext/xymon-plugin/
The installer, installed on a server.
.TP
.I $XYMONHOME/ext/xymon-plugin/tasks.cfg
Its task, which
.B enable
links into
.IR tasks.d/ ,
or on a client
.IR clientlaunch.d/ .
.TP
.I $XYMONTMP/xymon-plugin.host
On a client, the name its task sent the column under.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xymonapi (8)
